 "title": "A torus atom remembers exactly where its torus has no satisfying state: the atom rule for every class-forced free torus atom on any host",
 "subject": "Which grown handles hold the learned memory, and the atom rule beyond the Fano atom, separated atoms and octahedral spheres",
 "conclusion": "A torus atom grown on any orientable Kasteleyn knot space acts as its replaced line exactly where its torus has no satisfying state, transparent elsewhere, and holds a unit where it acts, whenever the torus is free at the removed point (proved by hand). Every lattice torus to 30 points is free (computed), so the Fano and thin-torus atoms of even index remember, the rest never do, and the memory does not need the Fano plane.",
